### 2. Updated `BaseFlow` (Enforce `templateName`)

Add validation in the constructor:

```java
package com.example.flow;

import com.example.service.DynamicPromptService;
import com.example.service.LlmService;
import org.springframework.ai.chat.messages.Message;

import java.util.List;

public abstract class BaseFlow implements Flow {

    protected final String flowIdentifier;
    protected final String promptText;
    protected final String vectorStoreName;
    protected final String knowledgeStoreName;
    protected final String templateName;

    public BaseFlow(String flowIdentifier, String promptText, String vectorStoreName, 
                    String knowledgeStoreName, String templateName) {
        if (flowIdentifier == null || flowIdentifier.trim().isEmpty()) {
            throw new IllegalArgumentException("flowIdentifier cannot be null or empty");
        }
        if (promptText == null || promptText.trim().isEmpty()) {
            throw new IllegalArgumentException("promptText cannot be null or empty");
        }
        if (templateName == null || templateName.trim().isEmpty()) {
            throw new IllegalArgumentException("templateName cannot be null or empty; every flow must have a prompt template");
        }

        this.flowIdentifier = flowIdentifier;
        this.promptText = promptText;
        this.vectorStoreName = vectorStoreName;
        this.knowledgeStoreName = knowledgeStoreName;
        this.templateName = templateName;
    }

    @Override
    public String getFlowIdentifier() {
        return flowIdentifier;
    }

    @Override
    public String getPromptText() {
        return promptText;
    }

    @Override
    public String getVectorStoreName() {
        return vectorStoreName;
    }

    @Override
    public String getKnowledgeStoreName() {
        return knowledgeStoreName;
    }

    @Override
    public String getTemplateName() {
        return templateName;
    }

    @Override
    public String execute(String userInput, String sessionId, List<Message> history, 
                          DynamicPromptService promptService, LlmService llmService) {
        String dynamicPrompt = promptService.buildPrompt(userInput, null, templateName, 
                                                        vectorStoreName, knowledgeStoreName, sessionId);
        String finalPrompt = promptText + "\n" + dynamicPrompt;
        return llmService.executePrompt(finalPrompt, sessionId);
    }
}
```

**Changes**:
- Added validation in the constructor to ensure `templateName` is non-null and non-empty.
- This enforces the requirement at instantiation time, catching issues when Spring creates the beans.

