### 3. Updated `FlowOrchestrator` (Additional Validation)

Add a runtime check for safety:

```java
package com.example.service;

import com.example.flow.Flow;
import org.springframework.beans.factory.annotation.Autowired;
import org.springframework.stereotype.Service;

import java.util.Map;

@Service
public class FlowOrchestrator {

    private final Map<String, Flow> flows;
    private final DynamicPromptService promptService;
    private final LlmService llmService;
    private final ConversationHistoryService historyService;

    @Autowired
    public FlowOrchestrator(Map<String, Flow> flows, DynamicPromptService promptService, 
                            LlmService llmService, ConversationHistoryService historyService) {
        this.flows = flows;
        this.promptService = promptService;
        this.llmService = llmService;
        this.historyService = historyService;
    }

    public String executeFlow(String flowIdentifier, String userInput, String sessionId) {
        Flow flow = flows.get(flowIdentifier + "Flow");
        if (flow == null || !flow.getFlowIdentifier().equals(flowIdentifier)) {
            throw new IllegalArgumentException("No flow found for flowIdentifier: " + flowIdentifier);
        }
        if (flow.getTemplateName() == null || flow.getTemplateName().trim().isEmpty()) {
            throw new IllegalStateException("Flow '" + flowIdentifier + "' is missing a prompt template");
        }

        List<Message> history = historyService.getHistoryBySessionId(sessionId);
        return flow.execute(userInput, sessionId, history, promptService, llmService);
    }
}
```

**Changes**:
- Added a runtime check to ensure `getTemplateName()` isn’t null or empty, providing a safety net if a custom flow bypasses `BaseFlow`.

